## Why This Is Asked
Tests the ability to design a safe, production-grade debugging workflow leveraging Time Travel and dbt macros while preserving tenant isolation and clear rollback.

## Key Concepts
- Tenant-scoped debug mirroring
- dbt macros for environment toggling
- Snowflake Time Travel for backfills
- CI gating and rollback strategies

## Code Example
```sql
{% macro swap_tenant_debug(tenant, mode) -%}
  {% if mode == 'debug' -%}
  create or replace view analytics_{{tenant}}.hourly_engagement as
  select * from analytics_{{tenant}}.debug_hourly_engagement;
  {% else -%}
  create or replace view analytics_{{tenant}}.hourly_engagement as
  select * from analytics_base.hourly_engagement;
  {% endif -%}
{%- endmacro %}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you safely expire old debug objects?
- How would you audit backfill changes across tenants?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests the ability to design a compliant, scalable data lifecycle with multi-tenant isolation, clear ownership, and automated governance in a dbt/Snowflake environment.

## Key Concepts
- dbt macros and run-operations for lifecycle management
- Snowflake Tasks and time-based scheduling
- Per-tenant Row-Level Security (RLS) isolation
- Data governance and CI gates for lifecycle policies

## Code Example
```sql
{% macro apply_retention(tenant, table) %}
  {% set policy = ref('retention_policies') | where('tenant = \''~tenant~'\' AND table_name = \''~table~'\'') | first %}
  {% set retention_days = policy.retention_days %}
  {% set archive_schema = policy.archive_schema %}

  {% set move_query %}
    INSERT INTO {{ archive_schema }}.archive_{{ table }}
    SELECT * FROM {{ this }}
    WHERE row_timestamp < DATEADD(day, -{{ retention_days }}, CURRENT_TIMESTAMP());

    DELETE FROM {{ this }}
    WHERE row_timestamp < DATEADD(day, -{{ retention_days }}, CURRENT_TIMESTAMP());
  {% endset %}

  {% do run_query(move_query) %}
{% endmacro %}
```
